<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The badge on the profile screen's "Password" row: a closed padlock.

    Closed rather than open, deliberately. An open padlock is the universal mark for "this is not
    protected", and the row it sits beside is the one that *changes* the password rather than one warning
    that something is unguarded — so a broken-open shackle here would say the opposite of the truth.

    See ic_profile_person.xml for why these badges are glyphs rather than the four-letter codes they
    replaced, and why none of them sets its own tint.
-->
